  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Cabin at Night",
    "overview": "Successor is a decision instrument dressed as the interior of the car it decides about: near-black cabin glass, hairline seams, one blue that lights only where a decision or focus lives, and small coloured telltales that report state the way a dashboard does. Numbers are readouts, not decoration; when a figure matters it is set wide and light like a gauge, and every figure can be opened down to the customer's words.\n\nDensity is high but calm (Fey-level restraint): one panel level, rules and whitespace instead of boxes in boxes, 12-14px working text, and a large wide headline only where a screen states its one question. Chrome floats over content rather than framing it: a translucent panoramic status band across the top, a floating dock at the bottom centre, ⌘K for everything, right-hand drawers for detail. The 3D car stage is the canvas for per-zone requirements and shares the same tokens.\n\nRejected by the build: the sidebar-of-pages admin dashboard, the card grid of identical KPI tiles, light mode, BMW logos.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Dark only; cabin black with a faint fixed blue glow in the top-left corner.",
      "One accent (decision blue) for the primary action, focus, PM-confirmed Must, and the active wave.",
      "Telltale colours (amber, red, green, violet) carry state, never decoration.",
      "Mona Sans on its width axis: normal width for reading, wide/light for instrument numerals.",
      "Proportional figures everywhere; tabular figures are deliberately off.",
      "One panel level, hairline borders, soft offset shadows only on floating layers."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The One Blue Rule",
        "body": "Blue means decision or focus. Solid Decision Blue appears on at most one action per view plus PM-confirmed Must marks; everything else blue is ink, wash or line.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Telltale Rule",
        "body": "Amber, red, green and violet only report state (conflict, fail, approved, challenged, evidence strength, delta direction). A telltale colour used for decoration is a false warning light.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Three-Step Tint Rule",
        "body": "Every state colour comes as solid (dot, bar, icon), ink (text), and a 13-16% wash (chip or note background). Never put solid-colour text on a wash.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Proportional Figures Rule",
        "body": "All numerals use proportional figures (`font-variant-numeric: proportional-nums`, `zero` and `ss01` off). Mona Sans's tabular set brings a code-style slashed zero; it is never switched on, including in tables and right-aligned columns.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Gauge Rule",
        "body": "Wide light numerals are earned: only a number the PM reads as a measurement (score, budget, count that matters) gets the instrument style. Labels and body numbers stay normal width.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The No-Kicker Rule",
        "body": "Headings stand alone: no eyebrow or kicker line above them, no section numbers, no gradient text. Context sits beside or below a title (meta line, chips), not stacked above it.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Floating Chrome Rule",
        "body": "Navigation never takes a column. The band floats on top, the dock floats at the bottom centre, detail opens in a right drawer, search lives in ⌘K. The page itself is all content.",
        "section": "layout"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Offset-Not-Halo Rule",
        "body": "Shadows are offset and soft-blurred black, never a coloured glow around an element. Telltale dots get a 3px tinted ring, which is the light's own lens, not a halo.",
        "section": "elevation"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Level Rule",
        "body": "A panel never sits inside a panel. Group inside a panel with whitespace, `.rule` hairlines and type.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do use solid Decision Blue for exactly one main action per view and for PM-confirmed Must marks.",
      "Do show any AI-originated priority as a dashed mark with the \"AI\" tag until a human confirms it.",
      "Do encode evidence with the four signal bars and scores with a bar or arc ticked at 45 and 60.",
      "Do report state with telltale dots and wash-plus-ink chips (amber conflict, red fail, green approved, violet challenged).",
      "Do set numerals in proportional figures; reserve wide (118%) light (300) numerals for genuine readouts.",
      "Do keep one panel level and group inside it with whitespace, hairline rules and type.",
      "Do float chrome (band, dock, ⌘K, right drawers) and keep the page all content; clear the band (52px) and dock (104px).",
      "Do use skeletons for loading, an error note with retry, and empty states that say what to do next.",
      "Do honour reduced motion; the duration tokens collapse to 0ms."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't add a sidebar of pages or a grid of identical icon-title-number KPI tiles.",
      "Don't turn on tabular figures or the slashed zero.",
      "Don't nest a panel inside a panel.",
      "Don't put a coloured stripe on the side of a card, row or note.",
      "Don't add eyebrow or kicker labels above headings, section numbers, gradient text or emoji.",
      "Don't use a telltale colour for decoration, or a coloured glow halo for emphasis.",
      "Don't introduce a light theme or any BMW logo or trademark.",
